        "original_id": "305b68fe-b9e8-5282-9d4e-f06d4afef9ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Chvrches, Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie\n- People: Lauren Mayberry, Iain Cook, Martin Doherty, Martin Metcalfe, John Duncan, Fin Wilson, Shirley Manson, Rona Scobie, Derek Kelly\n- Songs: \"Make Them Gold\"\n- Albums: Every Open Eye\n- Places: Bathgate, Edinburgh, Scotland\n\nFacts:\n- Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie was a Scottish rock group of the 1980s and 1990s that formed in Bathgate near Edinburgh, Scotland.\n- At Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie's commercial peak, the lineup included Martin Metcalfe on vocals, John Duncan on guitar, Fin Wilson on bass guitar, Shirley Manson and Rona Scobie on keyboards and backing vocals, and Derek Kelly on drums.\n- Chvrches consists of Lauren Mayberry, Iain Cook, and Martin Doherty.\n- Lauren Mayberry performs lead vocals, drums, additional synthesisers, and samplers in Chvrches.\n- Iain Cook performs synthesisers, guitar, bass, and vocals in Chvrches.\n- Martin Doherty performs synthesisers, samplers, and vocals in Chvrches.\n- \"Make Them Gold\" is a song by the Scottish synthpop band Chvrches from the band's second studio album Every Open Eye.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
